+Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5 is off. The ARN does not name the model. A
+profile on one of these models recovers at run time. The first
+structured-output request sends a forced tool choice. Bedrock rejects it once.
+Then the handle uses native output.
+
+Some requests fail locally before they reach Bedrock. These requests cannot
+teach the handle. Parallel first requests each get the rejection. A new handle
+pays the rejection again. Build one handle and clone it. This recovery is not
+verified live for application inference profiles.
